### Module Breakdown

#### Module 1 — Caltrans (Contractors Corner)
- **Type:** State, public, highly structured
- **Strengths:** Bid items, estimates, planholders, dates
- **Limitations:** Docs gated via NDA/login
- **Takeaway:** Gold standard for structured data

#### Module 2 — City of San Diego (PlanetBids)
- **Type:** SaaS procurement
- **Strengths:** Rich metadata, meetings, addenda
- **Limitations:** Docs gated
- **Takeaway:** Crawl-friendly, predictable

#### Module 3 — City of Irvine (PlanetBids)
- **Type:** Identical to Module 2
- **Takeaway:** One PlanetBids crawler supports many agencies

#### Module 4 — San Bernardino County (EPRO)
- **Type:** County-hosted
- **Strengths:** Mandatory job walk language, downloadable plans
- **Limitations:** Narrative-heavy
- **Takeaway:** High accessibility, strong risk signals

#### Module 5 — LADWP (ERSP)
- **Type:** Enterprise procurement
- **Strengths:** Dates, contacts, scope text
- **Limitations:** Docs gated, requirements embedded in prose
- **Key Correction:** No explicitly mandatory pre-bid or job walk
- **Takeaway:** Requires semantic parsing, not assumptions

#### Module 6 — LAWA (BonfireHub)
- **Type:** Modern SaaS procurement
- **Strengths:** Clean metadata, NAICS/commodity codes
- **Limitations:** Docs gated
- **Takeaway:** Metadata alone is highly valuable

#### Module 7 — RAMP LA (Aggregator + Gatekeeper)
- **Type:** Aggregator with eligibility gating
- **Strengths:** Estimates, scope, amendments, restrictions
- **Limitations:** Restricted primes, docs gated
- **Takeaway:** Eligibility ≠ availability

