### Module 2 — City of San Diego (PlanetBids) — Deep Dive

#### How We Got There (Discovery / Navigation Path)
- Navigation path:
  1. Googled **“City of San Diego vendor portal”**
  2. Landed on the City vendor registration page
  3. Clicked the CTA: **Vendor registration and bid opportunities**
  4. Arrived at a PlanetBids portal home page (URL indicates “portal-home”)
  5. Clicked **Bid Opportunities** to access the searchable list

**Portal Home:**  
- https://vendors.planetbids.com/portal/17950/portal-home

**Bid Opportunities List:**  
- https://vendors.planetbids.com/portal/17950/bo/bo-search

#### What We Observed on Bid Opportunities List Page
- The portal contains many categories beyond construction:
  - printing materials, hydrated lime, janitorial services, meal delivery, etc.
- This raised a pinned strategic thought:
  - BidBox *could* expand beyond construction eventually (government contracting broadly),
  - but we should avoid building “for everyone” too early.

#### Project Example Detail Page
- https://vendors.planetbids.com/portal/17950/bo/bo-detail/135924#bidInformation

#### What Information Was Available on the Project Detail Page (Tabbed)
**Bid Information tab**
- Bid due date/time
- Invitation / project number
- Categories / award categories
- License requirements
- Estimated bid value
- Bid bond information
- Pre-bid meeting details:
  - Meeting type (on-site)
  - Date/time
  - Attendance required (explicitly indicated)
- Contact info

**Line Items tab**
- Bid items line list (structured)

**Documents tab**
- Plans/specs downloadable (in this example, downloads were accessible with no login barrier observed)
- Addenda section with downloadable PDFs
- Email history section

**Prospective Bidders tab**
- A list/count of prospective bidders (planholders / registrants)

**Other UI Elements**
- “Remaining time” component (dynamic)
- Subcontractor ads section (none in the example)
- Bid results/awards (not yet)

#### Extraction Implications
- PlanetBids pages are:
  - Highly consistent across cities
  - Tabbed with stable anchors
  - Rich with structured metadata
- Even if docs are gated in some instances, the metadata usually is not.

#### Module 2 Bottom Line
- PlanetBids is a “platform module” — one parser can support many cities.
- Project detail pages expose the exact data BidBox needs: dates, meetings, addenda, line items.

